    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required emitting an audit line via the `AUDIT` logger on successful owner creation, carrying the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n\n**Added** `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/LogOwnerAudit.java` \u2014 a single-step function that reads the built `@Val Owner` and logs to the `AUDIT`-named SLF4J logger:\n\n```java\nprivate static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\");\n\npublic void service(@Val Owner owner) {\n    AUDIT.info(\"Owner created: id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n            owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n}\n```\n\n**Wired it into** `owners.POST.yml` as an `audit` step between `save` and `respond` (so the generated id is present and the response is unaffected), keeping it under the same `transaction` governance as its neighbours.\n\nThe audit line appears in the run \u2014 `AUDIT - Owner created: id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-11` \u2014 and `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` plus the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
